    slug: "gilmore-girls-netflixten-prime-videoya-tasindi",
    title: "End of an Era: 'Gilmore Girls' Leaves Netflix for Prime Video",
    excerpt: "A Netflix staple for 12 years, 'Gilmore Girls' moved to Prime Video as of July 1. Netflix retains the 2016 sequel series 'A Year in the Life.'",
    body: "An era has come to an end. Netflix's 12-year staple comfort show 'Gilmore Girls' has moved to Prime Video. The 2016 sequel series 'Gilmore Girls: A Year in the Life' will remain on Netflix; but the original seven seasons now sit on another platform's shelves.\n\nIn the show, Lauren Graham plays sharp-tongued Lorelai, while Alexis Bledel plays her diligent daughter Rory. The story of a mother and daughter \"growing up\" together in a small, quirky town interweaves Lorelai's young motherhood with Rory's high school and college years. Every supporting character is a cult favorite in their own right: Luke, whom Lorelai finally ends up with; her best friend Sookie; and the town's oddball, Kirk. The friends, rivals, and love interests who appear during Rory's school years add another layer to the show.\n\nThe show was beloved when it originally aired, but it's arguably even more popular now. Viewers especially love curling up with it in the fall: since the story's most beautiful moments are set in that season, it becomes a warm, comforting companion that helps dissolve the melancholy.\n\nShortly after 'Gilmore Girls' arrived on Netflix in 2014, the platform announced the four-episode, 90-minutes-each miniseries 'A Year in the Life.' Set roughly nine years after the original finale, this sequel installment will remain on Netflix. On the ancillary content front, there's still talk of the documentary 'Searching for Stars Hollow,' announced by Ink On Paper Studios for the show's 25th anniversary, though no release date has been set.\n\nIn short: 'A Year in the Life' stays on Netflix, but the original seven seasons of 'Gilmore Girls' have moved entirely to Prime Video. A note for anyone gearing up for their annual fall ritual: as of July 1, the show can only be watched on Prime Video.",
